  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **It Must Have Been The Roses**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **In The Midnight Hour**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n- **Playing In The Band Reprise**: back after 58 archived shows (567 days); rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2019-07-18.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 192 min [1]\n- **deadco2019-06-18.flac16**: source not stated; 20 songs; 192 min [2]\n- **deadandcompany2019-06-18.neumann_skm150.sunboy.flac16**: source not stated; 20 songs; 195 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The listener says the recording's filename date is wrong and the show actually took place on 6-18-2019 [4]\n- Lineup listed: Mickey Hart, Bill Kreutzmann, Bob Weir, Oteil Burbridge, Jeff Chimenti and John Mayer [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2019-07-18.flac24**: taped by Ed Guidry; transferred by Ed Guidry; source: (Lawn/Center) Neumann U89i (Hyper, DINA)> AETA PSP-3> Zoom F8 (24/48) on a SDHC Card. [1]. Also: Taped from lawn/center with Neumann U89i mics, run through AETA PSP-3 preamp into a Zoom F8 recording at 24-bit/48k onto SDHC card; Transferred from SDHC card via Mac Mini using Audacity and Fission, finished as 24/48 FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2019-06-18.flac16**: taped by Ed Guidry; transferred by Ed Guidry; source: (Lawn/Center) Neumann U89i (Hyper, DINA)> AETA PSP-3> Zoom F8 (24/48) on a SDHC Card. [2]. Also: Processed on a Mac Mini with Audacity and Fission, delivered as 16-bit/44.1k FLAC [2]\n- **deadandcompany2019-06-18.neumann_skm150.sunboy.flac16**: taped by Steven Weld; transferred by Steven Weld; source: Neumann SKM150(AK50's/LC3's/KM100's)>GAKables xlr>Lunatec V2>GAKables xlr>Apogee Mini-Me@24/96>AES/EBU>Sound Devices 722 @24bit/96kHz [3]. Also: Taper sat in section 8, row CC, seats 5 and 6, beside the left side of the mixer enclosure [3]",
